    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\mathbb R\\cap\\overline{\\left\\{\\dfrac{(2n+1)\\pi}{2}\\text{ where }n\\in\\mathbb Z\\right\\}}$, with complement relative to $\\mathbb R$.\n\nWrite odd integers as $2n+1$ and exclude their multiples of $\\frac{\\pi}{2}$.",
      "worked": "Every odd integer has the form $2n+1$, where $n\\in\\mathbb Z$. The excluded values therefore form $\\{\\frac{(2n+1)\\pi}{2}\\text{ where }n\\in\\mathbb Z\\}$. With $U=\\mathbb R$, the required set is\n$$\\mathbb R\\cap\\overline{\\left\\{\\frac{(2n+1)\\pi}{2}\\text{ where }n\\in\\mathbb Z\\right\\}}.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
